    "semantics": [
      "The added module is a scoring boundary with no executor, signer, dispatcher hook or automatic promotion. It returns scientific_admission=HOLD and production_authority=NONE in every result.",
      "Frozen manifests bind task pairs, independently declared clusters, environment sessions, arm order, horizon, decision/label chronology, source/model/evaluator identities, loss table and criteria. Duplicate environments, stale labels and type-confused booleans are rejected.",
      "Missing labels, costs and observations remain explicit and keep the planned denominator. Externally reviewable scoring requires complete original observations plus external receipt callbacks returning literal True; exceptions, missing callbacks and truthy strings fail closed.",
      "Whole-cluster sign flips use each cluster contribution to the same pair-weighted gain reported to the reviewer, including unequal cluster sizes. Terminal-error reduction must be strictly positive even if the frozen minimum is zero. Exact enumeration is bounded to20clusters, with maximum1000pairs.",
      "Historical engineering and CI archives retain their original failures, provenance and open gates; no historical CI/training result is relabeled as current integration qualification."
    ],
